<title>FRANCE: Paris Jan-April '97 import traffic up 3.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Paris Jan-April '97 import traffic up 3.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, in Jan-Apr 1997 totalled 179,171 tonnes, an increase of 3.6 percent on the same period last year, Aeroports de Paris (ADP),figures show.</p>
<p>The Paris airports January-April 1997 import traffic, in tonnes, by region, with percentage change on Jan-Apr 1996, was:</p>
<p>				 Tonnes   Pct change</p>
<p>    Domestic		  9,055   down  11.0</p>
<p>    European Union	 22,023     up  15.3</p>
<p>    Non-EU Europe	   4,135     up  10.8</p>
<p>    North Africa	    3,828   down  22.1</p>
<p>    Sub-Saharan Africa   19,251   down   0.3</p>
<p>    North America	  57,041   down   6.5</p>
<p>    French territories    5,507     up  10.8</p>
<p>    Latin America	   7,451     up  10.2</p>
<p>    Middle East	     8,397     up   0.1</p>
<p>    Far East		 42,483     up  23.2</p>
<p>    Total		   179,171     up   3.6</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
<p>www.racs.com</p>
</text>
